INHERITENCE-=====>

1->
Definition- Child class [derived class,sub claa] aquire/adopt/inherit the property and functionality of parent class [base class, super class]. Private member never inherited.
Syntax:
class Child_class_name : visibility_mode parent_class_name.

TYPES-=>

1->
Single- One child class inherited from only one parent class.
Syntax:
class parent
{
    code;
};
class child : public parent
{
    code;
};

2->
Multilevel- One class inherite other class whic is further inherited by another class.
Syntax:
class One
{
    code;
};
class other : public one
{
    code;
};
class another : public other
{
    code;
}

3->
Multiple- One child class inherite more than one parent class.
Syntax:
class parent1
{
    code;
};
class parent2
{
    code;
};
class child : public parent1, public parent2
{
    code;
}

4->
Heirarchical- more than one child class inherite one parent class.
Syntax:
class parent
{
    code;
};
class child1 : public parent
{
    code;
};
class child2 : public parent
{
    code;
}

